CORE
disjoint_port_drivers.sv
--top top --reset top.rst --undriven const --new-ic3 --witness-lasso 8
^\[top\.p_driven\] .*: PROVED$
^\[top\.p_gap_holds\] .*: PROVED$
^\[top\.p_gap_zero\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[top\.c_gap_000\] .*: PROVED$
^\[top\.c_gap_111\] .*: PROVED$
^\[top\.c_child_changes\] .*: PROVED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A child output drives [6:4] while the parent drives bits 7 and 0.
The undriven middle bits admit both extremes and hold their initial
value. All of these bits have one functional definition.
